WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Hi, my name is Stefan Gruenwedel.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.920
I'm an instructor on the Adobe Learn team.

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.560
In this video I'll show you the basics of Color Mode,

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.840
the brand new system for color grading

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.120
that's right inside Adobe Premiere.

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:15.324
To switch to Color Mode,

00:00:15.324 --> 00:00:18.000
click the Color tab at the top of the screen.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.949
The first thing you'll notice is the generous space

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:23.720
devoted to the program monitor in the middle.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.310
The clip grid on the right

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:28.240
displays each clip in the timeline.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.320
You can view them in a single column or as a grid.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.709
At the bottom are the various controls

00:00:37.709 --> 00:00:41.000
for color and contrast, color shift, and detail.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.674
As you click each control,

00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:47.240
a different heads-up display, or HUD, will appear.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:50.768
These displays show you what you're doing as you work,

00:00:50.768 --> 00:00:53.840
and they go away when you don't need them.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.440
Click once in a color control to display its HUD.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.297
Your mouse movements will then be constrained

00:01:00.297 --> 00:01:02.520
to adjust only that control.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:05.400
You don't have to hold the mouse button down either.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.708
Just drag the mouse up and down

00:01:07.708 --> 00:01:10.120
to adjust one parameter,

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:14.520
then drag it sideways to adjust another.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.184
You'll see a pop-up that says contrast changes

00:01:17.184 --> 00:01:19.600
are vertical, while pivot is horizontal.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.483
Pivot determines which part of the image

00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:22.480
is affected by the contrast adjustments.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:24.830
Hover over exposure, and you'll see that

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:29.083
vertical mouse movements control the exposure,

00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:32.440
while horizontal movements control the black level.

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:34.576
Hover over temperature, and you'll see that

00:01:34.576 --> 00:01:37.779
temperature adjustments go up and down,

00:01:37.779 --> 00:01:40.400
while side-to-side movements affect the tint.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.360
Play with each control group to get the hang of it.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.485
The changes are non-destructive, and you can always

00:01:48.485 --> 00:01:50.360
click reset to return things to where they were.

00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.655
Color shift auto samples the clip in the program monitor

00:01:54.655 --> 00:01:57.305
and extracts its dominant hues,

00:01:57.305 --> 00:02:00.320
as you can see from the hue swatches below the controls.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.029
As you click different clips in the clip grid,

00:02:03.029 --> 00:02:05.000
you'll see the swatches change.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:08.582
Click a swatch to adjust the hue and saturation

00:02:08.582 --> 00:02:11.000
of that color range.
